/-!
# The conductor of an algebra

For an algebra `B` over a commutative ring `A`, the **conductor** of `B` over `A` is the ideal

`𝔠 = {a ∈ A | a B ⊆ A} = Ann_A(B / A)`

of elements of `A` carrying all of `B` into the image of `A`. Here `B / A` is the quotient of `B`
by the image of `A`, an `A`-module but not in general a ring. When `A → B` is the normalization of
a reduced one-dimensional ring, this is the classical conductor of its singularities. Mathlib's
`conductor R x` is a different object: for `x` in an `R`-algebra `S` it is the largest ideal of
`S` contained in `R<x>`, an ideal of the larger ring, and it is defined only for the subalgebra
generated by one element.

When `B / A` is finite over `A`, the conductor commutes with localization: for a submonoid `S`
of `A`, the conductor of `S⁻¹B` over `S⁻¹A` is the extension of the conductor of `B` over `A`.
This compatibility lets the conductors of a finite morphism over affine opens of its target
glue to an ideal sheaf. Without finiteness only one inclusion holds.

For a subring `A` of a commutative ring `B` there is also the **ambient conductor**

`c(A, B) = {b ∈ B | b B ⊆ A}`,

an ideal of `B` rather than of `A`. It is the largest ideal of `B` contained in `A`, and for
`A = R<x>` it is Mathlib's `conductor R x`. Its contraction to `A` is the conductor of `B` over
`A` above. More generally, for any `A`-algebra `B` the conductor of `B` over `A` is the
contraction of the ambient conductor of the image of `A`, whether or not `A → B` is injective.
No finiteness, reducedness or birationality is assumed. The ambient conductor is a common ideal
of `A` and `B`, so `A` and `B` agree after inverting any element of `A` lying in it. This is the
affine form of Ferrand's pinching along the conductor.

## Main definitions

* `Subring.conductor A`: the ambient conductor of a subring `A` of `B`, the largest ideal of
  `B` contained in `A`.
* `TauCeti.Algebra.conductor A B`: the conductor of `B` over `A`, the annihilator of `B / A`.

## Main results

* `Subring.mem_conductor_iff`: `b ∈ c(A, B)` exactly when `b * x ∈ A` for every `x : B`.
* `Subring.le_conductor_iff`: an ideal of `B` lies in `c(A, B)` exactly when it is contained
  in `A`.
* `Subring.conductor_toSubring_adjoin_singleton`: for `A = R<x>` the ambient conductor is
  Mathlib's `conductor R x`.
* `Subring.image_comap_subtype_conductor`: the image of the contracted conductor is the
  ambient conductor, so the ambient conductor is a common ideal of `A` and `B`.
* `Subring.awayMap_subtype_bijective_of_mem_conductor`: for `t ∈ A` lying in `c(A, B)`, the map
  `A_t → B_t` is bijective.
* `TauCeti.Algebra.comap_conductor_range`: the conductor of `B` over `A` is the contraction of
  the ambient conductor of the image of `A`.
* `TauCeti.Algebra.map_conductor`: conversely, the extension of the conductor of `B` over `A` to
  `B` is the ambient conductor of the image of `A`; even its image is already that ideal
  (`TauCeti.Algebra.image_conductor`).
* `Subring.comap_subtype_conductor`: for a subring `A`, the conductor of `B` over `A` is the
  contraction of `c(A, B)`.
* `TauCeti.Algebra.conductor_eq_annihilator`: the conductor is the annihilator of `B / A`.
* `TauCeti.Algebra.mem_conductor_iff`: `a` lies in the conductor exactly when `a • b` lies in the
  image of `A` for every `b : B`.
* `TauCeti.Algebra.conductor_eq_colon`: the conductor is the colon ideal `(A : B)`.
* `TauCeti.Algebra.conductor_eq_top_iff`: the conductor is the unit ideal exactly when
  `A → B` is surjective.
* `TauCeti.Algebra.ker_algebraMap_le_conductor`: the kernel of `A → B` lies in the conductor.
* `TauCeti.Algebra.map_conductor_le`: the extension of the conductor to a localization
  lies in the conductor of the localization.
* `TauCeti.Algebra.conductor_eq_map`: for `B / A` finite over `A`, the conductor of a
  localization `S⁻¹B` over `S⁻¹A` is the extension of the conductor of `B` over `A`.
* `TauCeti.Algebra.conductor_eq_map_of_flat`: conductors commute with flat base change
  when `B / A` is finite; in particular this applies to finite algebras.

## References

* J.-P. Serre, *Algebraic Groups and Class Fields*, Chapter IV, §1, for the conductor of the
  normalization of a singular curve.
* D. Ferrand, *Conducteur, descente et pincement*, Bull. Soc. Math. France 131 (2003),
  Introduction and Théorème 5.1, for the ambient conductor of an arbitrary subring.
* [Stacks Project, Section 0ET0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0ET0), Lemma 37.14.1.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

namespace Subring

variable {B : Type*} [CommRing B] (A : Subring B)

/-- The **ambient conductor** `c(A, B)` of a subring `A` of a commutative ring `B`: the ideal of
`B` of the elements `b` with `b * x ∈ A` for every `x : B`. It is the largest ideal of `B`
contained in `A` (`Subring.le_conductor_iff`). -/
def conductor : Ideal B where
  carrier := {b | ∀ x, b * x ∈ A}
  zero_mem' x := by simp
  add_mem' ha hb x := by simpa only [add_mul] using A.add_mem (ha x) (hb x)
  smul_mem' c b hb x := by simpa only [smul_eq_mul, mul_left_comm, mul_assoc] using hb (c * x)

variable {A}

@[simp]
theorem mem_conductor_iff {b : B} : b ∈ A.conductor ↔ ∀ x, b * x ∈ A :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- The ambient conductor is contained in the subring. -/
theorem conductor_subset : (A.conductor : Set B) ⊆ A := fun b hb ↦ by
  simpa using mem_conductor_iff.mp hb 1

/-- **The conductor is the largest ideal contained in the subring.** -/
theorem le_conductor_iff {I : Ideal B} : I ≤ A.conductor ↔ (I : Set B) ⊆ A :=
  ⟨fun h ↦ (SetLike.coe_subset_coe.mpr h).trans conductor_subset,
    fun h _ hb ↦ mem_conductor_iff.mpr fun x ↦ h (I.mul_mem_right x hb)⟩

@[gcongr]
theorem conductor_mono {A' : Subring B} (h : A ≤ A') : A.conductor ≤ A'.conductor :=
  le_conductor_iff.mpr (conductor_subset.trans h)

/-- The ambient conductor is the unit ideal exactly when the subring is everything. -/
@[simp]
theorem conductor_eq_top_iff : A.conductor = ⊤ ↔ A = ⊤ := by
  refine ⟨fun h ↦ eq_top_iff.mpr fun b _ ↦ conductor_subset (h ▸ Submodule.mem_top), ?_⟩
  rintro rfl
  exact eq_top_iff.mpr fun b _ ↦ mem_conductor_iff.mpr fun _ ↦ Subring.mem_top _

@[simp]
theorem conductor_top : (⊤ : Subring B).conductor = ⊤ :=
  conductor_eq_top_iff.mpr rfl

/-- The ambient conductor of a subring of a field is zero exactly when the subring is proper. In
particular a proper subring has zero conductor, even when the field is finite over it. -/
@[simp]
theorem conductor_eq_bot_iff {K : Type*} [Field K] {A : Subring K} :
    A.conductor = ⊥ ↔ A ≠ ⊤ := by
  rw [Ne, ← conductor_eq_top_iff]
  exact ⟨fun h ↦ h ▸ bot_ne_top, (Ideal.eq_bot_or_top _).resolve_right⟩

/-- For the subalgebra `R<x>` generated by one element, the ambient conductor is Mathlib's
`conductor R x`. -/
theorem conductor_toSubring_adjoin_singleton (R : Type*) [CommRing R] [Algebra R B] (x : B) :
    (Algebra.adjoin R {x}).toSubring.conductor = _root_.conductor R x := by
  ext b
  simp [_root_.mem_conductor_iff]

/-- The image in `B` of the contracted conductor is the ambient conductor itself, not just the
ideal it generates. -/
theorem image_comap_subtype_conductor :
    A.subtype '' (A.conductor.comap A.subtype) = A.conductor :=
  Set.image_preimage_eq_of_subset fun b hb ↦ ⟨⟨b, conductor_subset hb⟩, rfl⟩

/-- Extending the contracted conductor back to `B` recovers the ambient conductor. -/
@[simp]
theorem map_comap_subtype_conductor :
    (A.conductor.comap A.subtype).map A.subtype = A.conductor := by
  refine le_antisymm Ideal.map_comap_le fun b hb ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩ := image_comap_subtype_conductor.symm.subset hb
  exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ha

variable (S Q : Type*) [CommRing S] [CommRing Q] [Algebra A S] [Algebra B Q] {t : A}
  [IsLocalization.Away t S] [IsLocalization.Away (A.subtype t) Q]

/-- **A subring and its ring agree away from the conductor.** If `t ∈ A` lies in the ambient
conductor `c(A, B)`, then the map `A_t → B_t` induced by the inclusion is bijective. -/
theorem awayMap_subtype_bijective_of_mem_conductor (ht : (t : B) ∈ A.conductor) :
    Function.Bijective (IsLocalization.Away.map S Q A.subtype t) := by
  have hker : RingHom.ker A.subtype ⊓ A.conductor.comap A.subtype = ⊥ := by
    rw [(RingHom.injective_iff_ker_eq_bot _).mp A.subtype_injective, bot_inf_eq]
  have hrange : ((A.conductor.comap A.subtype).map A.subtype : Set B) ⊆ Set.range A.subtype :=
    fun b hb ↦ ⟨⟨b, conductor_subset (Ideal.map_comap_le hb)⟩, rfl⟩
  exact IsLocalization.Away.map_bijective_of_mem_ideal S Q hker hrange ht

end Subring

namespace TauCeti.Algebra

variable (A B : Type*) [CommRing A] [Ring B] [Algebra A B]

/-- The **conductor** of an `A`-algebra `B`: the annihilator of the `A`-module `B / A`, the
quotient of `B` by the image of `A`. Its elements are the `a : A` with `a • B ⊆ A`
(`TauCeti.Algebra.mem_conductor_iff`). -/
def conductor : Ideal A :=
  Module.annihilator A (B ⧸ (1 : Submodule A B))

/-- The conductor is the annihilator of the quotient of `B` by the image of `A`. Under the module
system the body of `conductor` is not exported, so this is how importers unfold it. -/
theorem conductor_eq_annihilator :
    conductor A B = Module.annihilator A (B ⧸ (1 : Submodule A B)) :=
  (rfl)

/-- The conductor is the colon ideal `(A : B)` of `A` in `B`. -/
theorem conductor_eq_colon : conductor A B = (1 : Submodule A B).colon Set.univ :=
  Submodule.annihilator_quotient

variable {A B}

/-- An element `a : A` lies in the conductor exactly when it carries every element of `B` into
the image of `A`. -/
@[simp]
theorem mem_conductor_iff {a : A} :
    a ∈ conductor A B ↔ ∀ b : B, ∃ c : A, algebraMap A B c = algebraMap A B a * b := by
  simp [conductor_eq_colon, Submodule.mem_colon, Submodule.mem_one, Algebra.smul_def]

/-- The conductor is the unit ideal exactly when `A → B` is surjective. -/
@[simp]
theorem conductor_eq_top_iff : conductor A B = ⊤ ↔ Function.Surjective (algebraMap A B) := by
  simp [Ideal.eq_top_iff_one, Function.Surjective]

/-- The kernel of `A → B` lies in the conductor: an element mapping to zero carries `B` to
zero. -/
theorem ker_algebraMap_le_conductor : RingHom.ker (algebraMap A B) ≤ conductor A B :=
  fun a ha ↦ mem_conductor_iff.mpr fun _ ↦ ⟨0, by simp [(RingHom.mem_ker).mp ha]⟩

section BaseChange

variable (A) {B : Type*} [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]
  (A' B' : Type*) [CommRing A'] [CommRing B'] [Algebra A A']
  [Algebra A B'] [Algebra A' B'] [Algebra B B']
  [IsScalarTower A A' B'] [IsScalarTower A B B']
  [Algebra.IsPushout A A' B B'] [Module.Flat A A']
  [Module.Finite A (B ⧸ (1 : Submodule A B))]

/-- The conductor commutes with flat base change when `B / A` is finite, in particular
for finite algebras. The pushout formulation applies to any chosen realization of the
base-changed algebra. This follows from flat base change of annihilators (Stacks Tag 07T8). -/
theorem conductor_eq_map_of_flat :
    conductor A' B' = (conductor A B).map (algebraMap A A') := by
  let e := Algebra.IsPushout.equiv A A' B B'
  have hmap : (LinearMap.range ((Algebra.linearMap A B).baseChange A')).map
      e.toLinearMap = (1 : Submodule A' B') := by
    simp [← LinearMap.baseChange_range, ← Submodule.one_eq_range,
      Submodule.one_eq_span, Submodule.baseChange_span, Submodule.map_span,
      Algebra.IsPushout.equiv_tmul, e]
  let q := Submodule.Quotient.equiv _ _ e.toLinearEquiv hmap
  rw [conductor_eq_annihilator, ← q.annihilator_eq]
  rw [conductor_eq_annihilator, Submodule.one_eq_range]
  have : Module.Finite A (B ⧸ LinearMap.range (Algebra.linearMap A B)) := by
    rwa [← Submodule.one_eq_range]
  exact (Algebra.linearMap A B).cokernel_annihilator_flat_baseChange (S := A')

end BaseChange

section Localization

variable {B : Type*} [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]
variable (S : Submonoid A) (A' B' : Type*) [CommRing A'] [CommRing B'] [Algebra A A']
  [IsLocalization S A'] [Algebra B B'] [IsLocalization (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid B S) B']
  [Algebra A' B'] [Algebra A B'] [IsScalarTower A A' B'] [IsScalarTower A B B']

include S in
/-- The extension of the conductor of `B` over `A` to a localization `A'` of `A` lies in the
conductor of the corresponding localization `B'` of `B`. No finiteness is needed for this
inclusion. -/
theorem map_conductor_le :
    (conductor A B).map (algebraMap A A') ≤ conductor A' B' := by
  have h := IsLocalizedModule.map_annihilator_le S A'
    ((1 : Submodule A B).toLocalizedQuotient' A' S (IsScalarTower.toAlgHom A B B').toLinearMap)
  rwa [Submodule.localized'_one S A' B'] at h

include S in
/-- **The conductor commutes with localization.** If `B / A` is finite over `A`, `A'` is the
localization of `A` at a submonoid `S` and `B'` the localization of `B` at the image of `S`, then
the conductor of `B'` over `A'` is the extension of the conductor of `B` over `A`. -/
theorem conductor_eq_map [Module.Finite A (B ⧸ (1 : Submodule A B))] :
    conductor A' B' = (conductor A B).map (algebraMap A A') := by
  have := (Algebra.isPushout_of_isLocalization S A' B B').symm
  have : Module.Flat A A' := IsLocalization.flat A' S
  exact conductor_eq_map_of_flat A A' B'

end Localization

section Subring

variable {B : Type*} [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]

/-- **The conductor as a contracted ambient conductor.** The conductor of `B` over `A`, the
annihilator of `B / A`, is the contraction along `A → B` of the ambient conductor of the image
of `A`. This holds even when `A → B` is not injective. -/
theorem comap_conductor_range :
    (algebraMap A B).range.conductor.comap (algebraMap A B) = conductor A B := by
  ext a
  simp

/-- The image in `B` of the conductor of `B` over `A` is the ambient conductor of the image of
`A`, as a set: it is already an ideal of `B`. -/
theorem image_conductor :
    algebraMap A B '' conductor A B = (algebraMap A B).range.conductor := by
  rw [← comap_conductor_range, Ideal.coe_comap]
  exact Set.image_preimage_eq_of_subset fun b hb ↦ Subring.conductor_subset hb

/-- **The extended conductor.** Extending the conductor of `B` over `A` to `B` gives the ambient
conductor of the image of `A`, the largest ideal of `B` contained in that image. -/
theorem map_conductor :
    (conductor A B).map (algebraMap A B) = (algebraMap A B).range.conductor := by
  refine le_antisymm (comap_conductor_range (A := A) (B := B) ▸ Ideal.map_comap_le)
    fun b hb ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩ := image_conductor.symm.subset hb
  exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ha

end Subring

end TauCeti.Algebra

namespace Subring

variable {B : Type*} [CommRing B]

/-- For a subring `A` of `B`, the conductor of `B` over `A` is the contraction of the ambient
conductor `c(A, B)` to `A`. -/
theorem comap_subtype_conductor (A : Subring B) :
    A.conductor.comap A.subtype = TauCeti.Algebra.conductor A B := by
  rw [← TauCeti.Algebra.comap_conductor_range, Algebra.algebraMap_ofSubring, range_subtype]

end Subring
